 };
 
 // DCS Control (0070): how readily adaptive cadence passes frames through
@@ -1520,9 +1526,28 @@ struct CadenceConfig {
 //   steady    0032 as it was: enter at 0.80 of the period, leave over 0.95
 //             or on 2 missed-slot episodes within a second.
 //   balanced  enter at 1.10 (the estimate's excess over a real 0.9 or so);
-//             leave on 2 episodes within a second or 3 within 10 s.
-//   rate      enter at 1.25 (what may hold at all); leave on 2 episodes
-//             within a second only.
+//             leave on 3 episodes within a second or 5 within 10 s.
+//   rate      enter at 1.25 (what may hold at all); leave on 3 episodes
+//             within a second or 10 within 10 s.
+//
+// DCS Control (0071), from the first flights of 0070 (same view, 150 s each):
+//   - Smoothness buffer off, balanced: 1X held 28 s, 4 s and 17 s at a clean
+//     90 (no application frame over 16 ms, 4.5 ms of each period spent
+//     waiting in xrEndFrame) and was left each time on one hiccup of the
+//     runtime's own - its xrWaitFrame taking two periods twice, 165-210 ms
+//     apart - which 0070 read as two episodes within a second. Each exit
+//     then cost 30 s and more of 2 (the failed attempt's backoff). The
+//     application without the layer has the same hiccups and nobody counts
+//     them. So at 1X under these two preferences misses within 250 ms are one
+//     episode (one_late_episode_gap), and the counts are the ones above: a
+//     hiccup or two stay, a run of misses leaves within a second.
+//   - Smoothness buffer on (`pipelined_deep_hold`): the application ran at
+//     87 a second at 1X, unheld (xrEndFrame 0.5 ms), drifted past the 1X
+//     deadline and had a slot re-presented (407) every 100-270 ms: 1X does
+//     not hold there, and it was tried again at 30, 60, 120 s for a second
+//     or two of repeats each. An attempt that fails is now final sooner:
+//     balanced gives up after 3 failed in a row, rate after 6, until the
+//     scene changes (one_max_failed); steady retries as before.
 enum class CadencePreference : std::uint32_t { steady = 0, balanced = 1, rate = 2 };
 
